# RONDB-1124: an API close that crosses the end of a join aggregation
# after a receive timeout, and the next scan with the same transaction
# id (testJoinAggNdbApi Test 27).  DBTC error insert 8321 holds the end
# of the query until the API's close of it arrives, then ends the scan
# before it answers the close, and holds that answer (the second pure
# EndOfData of "Confirming scan close") until the API's next request on
# the same connection.  The DBUG keyword ndb_reduced_api_protocol_timeout
# cuts the API's wait for the end to 3 x 2 s.  The query must fail with
# 4008, the same query in a buddy transaction (Ndb::hupp(), same
# transaction id) after the close must give the right result, and the
# cluster must stay up.  Before the fix the buddy's scan reused the
# closed scan's connection and took the held answer as its own
# EndOfData: a debug NDB API aborted on assert(m_pendingWorkers > 0) in
# NdbQueryImpl::handleBatchComplete().  Debug only: the DBUG keyword
# needs a debug NDB API, and the error insert debug data nodes.
#
# A debug NDB API prints receive-timeout traces with timestamps while the
# query waits, so the program's output goes to a file and only its result
# lines are compared.  A crash fails the --exec; a failed check prints a
# FAILED line and "Some tests FAILED", which differ from the result file.
--source include/have_ndb.inc
--source include/have_debug.inc
--source include/have_ndb_debug.inc

--let $crossed_close_out = $MYSQLTEST_VARDIR/tmp/testJoinAggNdbApiCrossedClose.out
--echo Running testJoinAggNdbApi --only 27
--error 0,1
--exec $NDB_PUSH_AGG_DIR/testJoinAggNdbApi -c "$NDB_CONNECTSTRING" -m $MASTER_MYPORT --only 27 > $crossed_close_out 2>&1
--exec grep -E "^(Test 27|FAILED|All tests|Some tests)" $crossed_close_out
--remove_file $crossed_close_out

# DBTC clears 8321 in the TC instance that holds the end, and the
# program clears it everywhere, but not if it died: clear it here too.
# The mgm output goes to a test-local file that is removed again, so
# that check-testcase sees the same vardir before and after.
--let $crossed_close_mgm = $MYSQLTEST_VARDIR/tmp/testJoinAggNdbApiCrossedClose_mgm.log
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "all error 0" >> $crossed_close_mgm
--remove_file $crossed_close_mgm

# Clean up database created by test program
DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS test_db;
